  "description": "The Ti 420 is our all-purpose trail frame, capitalizing on short chainstays and designed with more versatility than any other similar frame. Ti softens the blows and drops the weight, while 420mm chainstays ensure snappy handling. Paragon Machine Works sliding dropout inserts allow for any combination of brake mounts, axle types and gearing you can think of, from black anodized thru axle with 74mm post mounts to silver Rohloff-specific with 51mm disc tabs.\n\nOur most recent iteration of the frame features clamp-on cable guides on the underside of the downtube for a cleaner look and the ability to customize the number of housing sections you’re using. And of course, there is a port for internal dropper routing.\n\nWant to try 27.5 or 27.5+? No problem! The 420 has a slightly higher-than-average bottom bracket height, allowing it to handle 27.5 wheels without bringing the bottom bracket height too low.\n\nIf you’re looking to run fatter tires like 29 x 2.8 or 3″, check out our Gnarvester 29+ frame!\n\nIs there a little detail you don’t like? Want to tweak the geometry a bit? Have a cool idea for a frame? As with all our titanium frames, customization is no problem. For an extra $400 we can edit this frame to your liking, or start completely from scratch. Contact us any time and let us know what you’re looking for. We can help you design a frame and give you an accurate timeline for how long it will take to build.",
